WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:03.188
Everything ends in evidence
an assessor can inspect.

2
00:00:03.188 --> 00:00:08.529
The baseline is one dated export of the
labels, label policies, auto-labeling,

3
00:00:08.529 --> 00:00:13.700
D L P, audit status and the Rights
Management configuration, taken monthly.

4
00:00:13.700 --> 00:00:17.046
Drift is any difference no
change ticket explains,

5
00:00:17.046 --> 00:00:21.825
and drift that weakens a control on C
U I goes to the authorizing official.

6
00:00:21.825 --> 00:00:26.331
The book carries three rows of the
Zero Trust Assessment closure map,

7
00:00:26.331 --> 00:00:28.387
each with its minimum evidence.

8
00:00:28.387 --> 00:00:33.650
No labels, defaults or containers needs
a policy export and a labeled sample.

9
00:00:33.650 --> 00:00:36.499
Rights Management and
mail encryption need an

10
00:00:36.499 --> 00:00:39.275
encrypted test and the
transport-rule export.

11
00:00:39.275 --> 00:00:42.225
Audit gaps need searchable
synthetic events.

12
00:00:42.225 --> 00:00:45.473
And the metrics measure
protection, not settings:

13
00:00:45.473 --> 00:00:50.227
the labeled share of sensitive content,
container coverage of C U I sites,

14
00:00:50.227 --> 00:00:53.475
true-positive and override
rates, and test passes.

15
00:00:53.475 --> 00:00:57.988
A policy that's on and catches nothing
scores no better than one that's off.

16
00:00:57.988 --> 00:01:00.890
The package supports
the controls it maps to;

17
00:01:00.890 --> 00:01:04.010
the assessor or authorizing
official decides.
